# CSS Architecture Alignment

#>spw_css_architecture_alignment
#:review #!css #!semantics #!architecture
#:layer #!pragmatics

@style_css: ~"../../../public/css/style.css"
@css_instruction: ~"../../conventions/css-instruction.spw"
@tokens_core: ~"../../../public/css/tokens/core.css"
@grammar_syntax: ~"../../../public/css/grammar/syntax.css"
@handles_operators: ~"../../../public/css/handles/operators.css"
@effects_wonder: ~"../../../public/css/effects/wonder.css"
@ornament: ~"../../../public/css/ornament/ornament.css"
@spw_css_architecture_plan: ~"../../.agents/plans/spw-css-architecture/PLAN.md"
@runtime_bootstrap_plan: ~"../../.agents/plans/runtime-bootstrap-performance/PLAN.md"
@selector_timing_review: ~"./runtime-audit/selector-timing-chunking-musical-ontology.spw"
@runtime_audit_index: ~"./runtime-audit/index.spw"
@site_semantics: ~"../../conventions/site-semantics.spw"
@attention_field: ~"../../conventions/attention-field.spw"

thesis: .{
  claim = `The CSS architecture has strong layering and good data-attribute hygiene, but the semantic model expressed in CSS is not yet fully aligned with the runtime's Spw ontology (operators as forces, frames/braces as structural grammar, regions as harmony/tempo/density, attention-field as resonance, cauldron as emergence).`
  opportunity = `Redistributing ownership and evolving the file tree can make CSS a clearer, more direct projection of the same semantics that the JS runtime and .spw surfaces already model.`
  constraint = `The current strict layer order (reset → tokens → shell → typography → grammar → components → systems → routes → handles → effects → ornament) remains the default contract. Later fundamentals-practice-rhythms work opens the door to layer-order review, but only as a standalone migration with evidence, updated AGENTS.md/css-instruction.spw/style.css imports, and rollback notes.`
}

# Current State of Semantic Alignment

strengths: .{
  layering = `The @layer declaration and import order in style.css precisely matches the documented contract in AGENTS.md.`
  tokens = `tokens/core.css contains excellent runtime-facing @property declarations and operator color contracts that already think in Spw terms.`
  data_attributes = `Significant and correct use of data-spw-* selectors (especially operator, form, gesture, wonder-state, cauldron-phase) in higher layers.`
  field_projection = `:has() usage for live gesture/brace/cauldron and resonance states successfully makes CSS "listen" to the runtime attention model.`
  instruction_contract = `css-instruction.spw already encodes the correct principles (body[data-spw-surface] as page truth, prefer existing data-spw-* families, debug contracts, ownership boundaries).`
  partial_musical = `Rhythm tokens (--spw-site-rhythm-tempo, --spw-site-rhythm-density) and region harmony/tempo/density are generated by the runtime and lightly consumed in ornament.`
}

friction_points: .{
  grammar_underpowered = `Core brace physics, frame delimiter logic, and sigil-as-semantic-handle behavior have leaked upward into handles/operators.css and multiple route files.`
  field_semantics_too_high = `The continuous "resonant field" projection lives primarily in handles/operators.css and effects/wonder.css rather than having a clearer home closer to grammar or systems.`
  musical_projection_weak = `The rich musical metaphors already present in the runtime (boonhonk as 5-voice mixer, cauldron as gather/mix/garden, rhythm/harmony tokens, operator voices) have almost no systematic visual grammar outside ornament.`
  defensive_overrides = `Scattered !important rules in grammar/syntax.css and handles/ (mostly for inspect/reset states) indicate semantic friction rather than clean state modeling.`
  route_bloat = `Several large route CSS files still carry reusable operator, brace, frame, and region logic that duplicates patterns better owned lower in the cascade.`
  selector_timing_mismatch = `We now have explicit modeling of staged JS selector evaluation (see selector_timing_review). The CSS side (complex :has(), attribute chains) has continuous cost but no equivalent documented posture per layer.`
}

# Opportunities to Align Semantics Differently

opportunities: .{
  treat_grammar_as_first_class = `Move structural brace/frame/delimiter/sygil semantics down into grammar/ so that "what a thing is" is expressed at the grammatical layer rather than the handle or route layer.`
  give_field_projection_a_home = `Create a dedicated, low-specificity surface whose sole responsibility is projecting the current attention-field / wonder / resonance / cauldron state. This makes the continuous CSS field a peer to the staged JS runtime chunks.`
  elevate_musical_rhythmic_semantics = `Make harmony, tempo, density, rhythm, and cauldron phase first-class visual concerns in systems/ (not just ornament). This would make the "runtime as instrument" legible in the visual layer in a way that matches the workbench metaphysics and recent ontology work.`
  express_inspect_states_via_data = `Replace many defensive !important resets with explicit data-spw-inspect-mode or data-spw-debug-* attributes written by the runtime, styled cleanly in a dedicated (still low) location.`
  slim_routes_via_extraction = `Push duplicated operator/brace/region patterns out of route files into grammar or systems so that route CSS becomes true surface personality only.`
  document_selector_posture = `Add explicit guidance (in css-instruction.spw or a small new note) about intended selector cost and complexity per layer — grammar and systems should stay cheap and direct; complex field logic belongs higher.`
}

# Redistribution Proposals (Layer-Respecting)

redistribution: .{
  grammar_layer = `Expand grammar/ to own more of the structural contract:
    - Consider grammar/structure.css or grammar/frames-braces.css for core frame, brace, delimiter, and sigil semantics (currently scattered).
    - Keep grammar/syntax.css focused on token-level syntax coloring and operator typography.
    - This moves "what these elements mean structurally" down the cascade where it belongs.`

  systems_layer = `Introduce clearer ownership for semantic projection:
    - systems/field-projection.css (or systems/semantic-projection/) for the attention-field, wonder, resonance, and cauldron state mapping.
    - systems/rhythm.css (light) for consumption of --spw-site-rhythm-*, region harmony/tempo/density as visual grammar and motion parameters.
    - This creates a natural home for the "musical projection" that currently only lives in ornament and a few runtime-state files.`

  handles_layer = `Narrow the charter:
    - handles/ should focus on interaction affordances and cognitive chrome (phase controls, cognitive handles, logo behavior).
    - Large amounts of operator color state, gesture projection, and field resonance currently living in handles/operators.css can move down to grammar/ or the new field-projection surface.`

  effects_layer = `Keep effects/ for ambient, additive, non-structural projection (material, grain, electromagnetic, narrative, wonder as celebration).
    - The new field-projection work could live here if it stays strictly additive, or in systems/ if it is considered core semantic infrastructure.`

  routes_layer = `Aggressive slimming:
    - Audit blog, settings, rpg-wednesday, design-experiments, and other large route files.
    - Extract any reusable operator/brace/region/frame logic into grammar or systems.
    - Routes should primarily own palette personality, layout rhythm, and surface-specific delight.`

  ornament_layer = `Protect its charter:
    - Ornament remains the highest layer for whimsy, relational-state celebration, and non-essential atmospheric projection.
    - It should consume the new field and rhythm systems rather than duplicating their logic.`
}

# File Tree Evolution Options

file_tree_ideas: .{
  conservative = `Stay within current directories but redistribute files:
    - public/css/grammar/structure.css (new)
    - public/css/systems/field-projection.css (new)
    - public/css/systems/rhythm.css (new or light)
    - Move targeted sections out of handles/operators.css and large route files.`

  moderate = `Light structural growth:
    - public/css/grammar/
        syntax.css (existing)
        structure.css (new — frames, braces, delimiters, sigils)
    - public/css/systems/
        surfaces/ (existing)
        field-projection.css (new)
        rhythm.css (new)`

  bolder = `Clarify the semantic projection split:
    - Introduce public/css/systems/semantic-projection/ as a sub-area for anything that maps runtime state (attention, wonder, resonance, cauldron, rhythm) into visual grammar.
    - This makes the "projection" nature of the architecture more visible in the filesystem, aligning with precipitates-and-projections.spw thinking.`

  invariants = `Any tree change must:
    - Preserve the current layer order in style.css unless the patch is explicitly a layer-order migration.
    - Keep css-instruction.spw as the active contract for new or moved files.
    - Not create new layers without documenting why existing layers cannot express the semantic flow.
    - Make it easier (not harder) for an editor to answer "where does X semantic concern live?"`
}

# Connection to Broader Work

connections: .{
  runtime = `This review is the CSS mirror of the selector timing + chunking ontology work (selector_timing_review) and the runtime-bootstrap-performance plan. Staged JS evaluation and continuous CSS field projection should be understood as two sides of the same semantic model.`
  musical = `The musical projection (operators as voices, cauldron as mixer, rhythm/harmony as arrangement, attention-field as resonant space) is already latent in the runtime and workbench metaphysics. CSS can become a much stronger participant in that projection.`
  workbench = `The spw-workbench models Spw as a language with explicit grammar, physics, and projection mechanics. The site's CSS architecture should feel like one coherent projection of that same language rather than a parallel styling system.`
  prior_plan = `This continues the intent of spw-css-architecture/PLAN.md (making braces and operators first-class semantic primitives) with fresh context from runtime performance and ontology work.`
}

# Recommended Path (Smallest Honest Surfaces)

recommended_path: .{
  phase_0 = `Create this review artifact and wire it into reviews/index.spw and the spw-css-architecture plan.`
  phase_1 = `Strengthen grammar/ with structural brace/frame/delimiter ownership (small extraction from handles and 1-2 route files).`
  phase_2 = `Introduce a focused field-projection surface (new file under systems/ or effects/) and begin routing attention/wonder/resonance/cauldron state through it.`
  phase_3 = `Elevate rhythmic and musical tokens into systems/ with a small rhythm or semantic-projection file; increase their consumption in components and systems.`
  phase_4 = `Audit and slim the largest route CSS files against the new grammar + field surfaces.`
  phase_5 = `Address defensive !important patterns via explicit data attributes + clean styling in the appropriate layer.`

  validation = `After each phase: css-instruction.spw compliance, git diff --check, npm run check (or the CSS subsets), and manual review on representative routes (home, blog, topics/software, a settings surface, rpg-wednesday). For ordinary redistribution, preserve layer order. For an explicit layer-order migration, include AGENTS.md + style.css + .spw convention updates and a rollback note.`
}

# Status

status: .{
  created = `During CSS architecture review following selector timing, chunking ontology, and musical runtime considerations (2026-04).`
  wired = `Referenced from reviews/index.spw and spw-css-architecture/PLAN.md.`
  next = `Use as the canonical reference for any redistribution work. Update as concrete extractions land.`
  evolved = `Extended by modular-experience-slices-volleyball.spw and fundamentals-practice-rhythms.spw. The latter adds practice beds, names math-practice-labs as the first concrete pilot, and reframes CSS layer-order changes as possible but evidence-gated migrations rather than routine redistribution.`
}
